# OmniCompost — short-URL redirects for printed-guide QR codes.
# Format: Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` (one rule per line:  from  to  status).
#
# The QR codes on the printed guides encode STABLE short URLs (/g/<slug>), never the
# PDF's real path. The host 302-redirects each short URL to the current hosted PDF, so a
# card printed today keeps resolving after the PDF is re-exported. Keep the slug forever;
# change only the target on the right. Use 302 (temporary) so scanners/browsers never
# cache an old target; promote to 301 only if a destination is truly permanent.

/g/kitchen          /assets/guides/kitchen-guide-v5.pdf      302
/g/lawn             /assets/guides/lawn-guide-v6.pdf         302
/g/troubleshooting  /assets/guides/troubleshooting-guide.pdf 302
/g/compost          /can-i-compost                           302

# The first three target the rendered print PDFs in assets/guides/. Swap a right-hand
# side if a final Canva re-export lands under a new filename; the /g/<slug> on the left
# stays fixed so already-printed cards keep resolving.
# /g/compost is the searchable "Can I Compost This?" page (can-i-compost.html, generated
# from field-guides/items.json by build_mobile.py). 302 until the URL is final; promote to
# 301 once it's printed on stickers/guides.

